    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4900" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">balsămum</span></b> , i,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάλσαμον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A fragrant gum of the balsam-tree</i>, <i>balsam</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 2,
				119</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 13, 1, 2, § 8 sq.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">balsama olet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					3, 63</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tac.
				G. 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 36, 3</span></i>: <i><span class="en">Vulg. Ezech.
				27, 17</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The balsam-tree</i>: Amyris opobalsamum, Linn.;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				12, 25, 54, § 111</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sol.
				35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 5, 6</span></i>.</div>
